PRODUCTION OF MEMORY CHIPS

*145.  SHRI CHAMALA KIRAN KUMAR REDDY:
SHRI EATALA RAJENDER:

Will the Minister of ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY be pleased to state:

(a) whether the Government expects more companies to start production of memory chips in the country and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether there is a global phenomenon of supply-demand imbalance which is now getting addressed by setting many more data centres;
(c) if so, whether new companies are likely to invest in the country to manufacture memory chips while existing investors are likely to scale up production to address the demand-supply gap in the segment and if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether strong demand for memory (data storage) cards and advanced chips has tightened global supplies and supported higher prices in past quarters and manufacturers have been sprucing up investments and production capacities to meet market requirements worldwide and the higher memory chip prices have, in turn, led to a rise in production costs for a range of electronic products including smartphones and laptops; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?
